<BaseLayout title="About — Ben Kennedy">
  <main><div class="container page-hero"><div class="eyebrow">About</div><h1>Network engineering is the primary discipline. Automation is the multiplier.</h1><p>I’m a UK-based network engineer working across a broad production estate spanning routing, switching, wireless, security, identity and observability. I’m most interested in technically demanding environments where deep networking knowledge and automation meet.</p></div>
  <section class="section"><div class="container grid-2"><div class="card"><h3>Production background</h3><p>Hands-on operational experience with Cisco enterprise networking, Palo Alto firewalls, Cisco ISE, Catalyst Center, ThousandEyes, PRTG and the day-to-day realities of troubleshooting live infrastructure.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Automation background</h3><p>Designed and deployed an internal Flask-based automation application used by the network team. My focus is practical automation: reducing repetitive work, integrating platforms and creating safer operational workflows.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Current direction</h3><p>Working toward CCIE Enterprise Infrastructure while deliberately adding Linux, Arista, multicast, EVPN/VXLAN, packet analysis and infrastructure automation.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Long-term target</h3><p>London-based financial-markets, trading or fintech infrastructure — environments with strong engineering culture, large-scale networks and difficult technical problems.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="callout">Public portfolio material is deliberately sanitized. No employer-confidential configs, addressing, topology, screenshots or internal operational data are published here.</div></div></section></main>
